# `f a > b` reads by the fit of f's parameter, never by where the phrase stands (card parse-so, decision juxtaposition)
'xs=[1,2]; ok = all xs > 0; ok'	yes
'xs=[1,-2]; if all xs > 0 {1} else {0}'	0
'xs=[1,2,3,4]; ok = count xs > 3; ok'	yes
'xs=[1,2]; ok = max xs > 0; ok'	yes
# a function of an untyped parameter before a comparison reads two ways: refused, naming both (decision untyped-fit-ambiguous)
'sq(x) := x*x; sq 2 == 4'	error
'sq(x: int) := x*x; sq 2 == 4'	yes
'sq(x) := x*x; (sq 2) == 4'	yes
